    "note": "REAL intraday data, not interpolated -- Dukascopy retains tick-level history for EURUSD back to the early 2000s. Prices are mid = (bid+ask)/2 from real ticks, binned into 30-minute candles. EUR/USD was trading near parity this week (~1.00-1.03), consistent with the well-documented mid-2022 parity approach. Decision text published 13:15 CEST / 11:15 UTC (marker); Lagarde press conference followed at 13:45 CEST / 11:45 UTC. Press reports describe EUR/USD spiking to 1.0257 then extending to 1.0277 on the surprise +50bp size before fading back under 1.02 as the press conference flagged a weaker growth outlook -- that fade-back is visible in this series through the afternoon of 2022-07-21."
